          }
          definition {
            value: "The Absolute URL for the resource.  The fullUrl SHALL NOT disagree with the id in the resource - i.e. if the fullUrl is not a urn:uuid, the URL shall be version-independent URL consistent with the Resource.id. The fullUrl is a version independent reference to the resource. The fullUrl element SHALL have a value except that: \n* fullUrl can be empty on a POST (although it does not need to when specifying a temporary id for reference in the bundle)\n* Results from operations might involve resources that are not identified."
          }
          comment {
            value: "fullUrl might not be [unique in the context of a resource](bundle.html#bundle-unique). Note that since [FHIR resources do not need to be served through the FHIR API](references.html), the fullURL might be a URN or an absolute URL that does not end with the logical id of the resource (Resource.id). However, but if the fullUrl does look like a RESTful server URL (e.g. meets the [regex](references.html#regex), then the \'id\' portion of the fullUrl SHALL end with the Resource.id.\n\nNote that the fullUrl is not the same as the canonical URL - it\'s an absolute url for an endpoint serving the resource (these will happen to have the same value on the canonical server for the resource with the canonical URL)."
          }
